# List Card Layout

Use shared layout primitives from `@/components/common/ListCardLayout` and `@/components/common/CardKebabTrigger` for list-page cards. Step-by-step skill: [card-list-item-ui](../skills/card-list-item-ui/SKILL.md). Pair with [system-kebab-menu.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/system-kebab-menu.mdc) for menu items and [list-pages-card-view.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-pages-card-view.mdc) for grid breakpoints.

## Grid vs list

- **Grid card:** use `LIST_CARD_GRID_SHELL` (or domain wrapper that composes it)
- **List row:** use `LIST_CARD_LIST_SHELL` with `ListCardMediaColumn` + `ListCardContent`

Both modes should accept `viewMode: "grid" | "list"` on the same card component when possible.

## No duplicate values

Each fact appears once per card (per view branch). Do not repeat title, description, status, the same price, tags, or contact fields in header, hero overlay, detail grid, and footer. Grid price: hero overlay **or** body meta, not both. Skill: [card-list-item-ui](../skills/card-list-item-ui/SKILL.md).

## List row structure

```
[ListCardMediaColumn]  [ListCardContent]
                         ListCardDetailsHeader (title, status badge, kebab)
                         LIST_CARD_DETAIL_GRID_CLASS (detail fields)
                         LIST_CARD_DETAIL_DIVIDER_CLASS (optional)
                         footer (price, dates, actions)
```

Shared class exports from `ListCardLayout.tsx`:

- `LIST_CARD_DETAIL_GRID_CLASS` — `grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-x-4 gap-y-3`
- `LIST_CARD_DETAIL_DIVIDER_CLASS` — low-contrast separator between detail blocks

## Media helpers

- `ListCardCoverImage` — full-bleed cover in media column
- `ListCardBlurredMedia` — blurred background + centered avatar/logo (grid hero style)
- `ListCardContactRow` — phone/email rows with Lucide icons

## Kebab placement

Use `CardKebabTrigger` with the correct variant:

- **`overlay`** — on photo/dark media (compact dark trigger)
- **`default`** — in list header row on light surfaces

Always `stopPropagation` on trigger and menu content (see kebab-menu rule).

## Status badges

Use `statusBadgeClasses` from `@/shared/utils/statusBadges` with `Badge` — see [status-badges.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/status-badges.mdc). Do not inline ad-hoc Tailwind color strings per card.

## Reusable cards

When a card is used across features, promote to `@/shared/components/<domain>/` and register in showcase ([component-showcase.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/component-showcase.mdc)).

